From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] docs: build man pages only when docs are enabled

docs/ is entered unconditionally and its man pages are built regardless of the
docs option, so a build that asked for no documentation still stops here:

  docs/meson.build:15:4: ERROR: Unable to find Docbook XSL stylesheets for
  man pages

The stylesheets have to be present locally and reachable through an XML
catalog, since the sheet is named by its docbook.sourceforge.net URL and
--nonet forbids fetching it. Buildroot has no docbook-xsl package at all, so
this would mean adding one, plus the catalog wiring, to produce files that
Buildroot's target-finalize then deletes - it removes
$(TARGET_DIR)/usr/share/man unconditionally.

Put the man pages behind the same docs option as the handbook and the API
documentation. With -Ddocs=true the behaviour is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/docs/meson.build
+++ b/docs/meson.build
@@ -8,6 +8,15 @@
 as_doc_target_dir = join_paths(get_option('datadir'), 'doc', 'appstream')
 
 # make manual pages
+#
+# Behind the docs option, along with everything else here. Building these
+# needs xsltproc and a local copy of the Docbook XSL stylesheets, resolved
+# through an XML catalog, and a build that has asked for no documentation
+# should not fail for want of them:
+#
+#   ERROR: Unable to find Docbook XSL stylesheets for man pages
+if get_option('docs')
+
 manpages_xsl = 'http://docbook.sourceforge.net/release/xsl/current/manpages/docbook.xsl'
 xsltproc = find_program('xsltproc')
 if run_command([xsltproc, '--nonet', manpages_xsl],
@@ -51,6 +60,8 @@
     )
 endif
 
+endif # docs
+
 if get_option('docs') or get_option('apidocs')
   # we need Python for the helper scripts if any doc generation is enabled at all
   python_exe = find_program('python3', 'python')
